== Kit ==
Since it was started in 1928, Real Valladolid has always had a home uniform of purple and white stripes. This uniform was picked to make sure it wasn't too similar to other early clubs,  and they still use the same basic design with very few changes. Purple and white have become the team's colors, and they're a big part of the club's story.<ref>{{Cite web |title=historia real valladolid cf :: La Futbolteca. Enciclopedia del Fútbol Español |url=http://lafutbolteca.com/tag/historia-real-valladolid-cf/ |access-date=2024-03-24 |language=ES-es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Guallar |first=Javi |date=2013-12-03 |title=CAMISETAS SPORT CLUB: R. VALLADOLID C.F. |url=http://camisetassportclub.blogspot.com/2013/12/r-valladolid-cf.html |access-date=2024-03-24}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Tercera Camiseta Valladolid 1999-00 |url=https://www.footballkitarchive.com/es/valladolid-1999-00-third-kit/ |access-date=2024-03-24 |website=Football Kit Archive |language=es-ES}}</ref>

During the 2012–13 season, Real Valladolid showed their support for [[Madrid]]'s bid to host the [[2020 Summer Olympics|2020 Olympics]] by wearing a special shirt for their match against [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] at the [[Santiago Bernabéu Stadium]]. The shirt featured black and purple stripes with eye-catching orange numbers on the back.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Presentada la camiseta del Real Valladolid en apoyo a Madrid 2020.{{!}} Cadena Ser |url=https://cadenaser.com/emisora/2013/05/03/radio_valladolid/1367537293_850215.html |access-date=2013-05-03 |website=Cadena Ser - Web Oficial |date=3 May 2013 |language=es}}</ref>

On September 24, 2023, Real Valladolid had to play their match at the [[Estadio Carlos Tartiere|Carlos Tartiere Stadium]] against [[Real Oviedo]] wearing a fourth kit. This is because the Technical Committee of Referees (CTA) considered that the three kits of the pucelano team have violet as the predominant color and considered that they are similar to the first kit of the Asturian team, despite having played other seasons with the first kit, replacing the white shorts with violet ones.<ref>{{Cite web |title=El Pucela jugará con camiseta y medias amarillas, y con pantalón violeta de la segunda equipación en el estadio Carlos Tartiere CTA de la RFEF no permitirá que el Real Valladolid utilice ninguna de sus tres equipaciones oficiales por considerar que hay una similitud de tono y/o color con la primera del Real Oviedo{{!}} Twitter (Real Valladolid C.F.) |url=https://twitter.com/realvalladolid/status/1705598084221182027?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1705598084221182027%7Ctwgr%5Ed730eab269eff2b4b1d621743056255b079c6331%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fvipdeportivo.es%2Freal-oviedo-real-valladolid-las-novedades%2F |access-date=2023-09-23 |website=Twitter (Real Valladolid C.F.) - Web Oficial |language=es}}</ref> The Promesas wore their previously mentioned kit without issue during their [[Segunda Federación]] match against [[Real Oviedo Vetusta]] last week.<ref>{{Cite web |title=0-1: La primera, con el sello de Arnu. El Real Valladolid Promesas venció al Real Oviedo Vetusta, disputado en El Requexón, en Oviedo, el domingo 17 de septiembre de 2023.{{!}} Real Valladolid C.F. |url=https://www.realvalladolid.es/noticias/0-1-la-primera-con-el-sello-de-arnu |access-date=2023-09-17 |website=Real Valladolid C.F. - Web Oficial |language=es}}</ref> This kit consisted of a yellow shirt and socks, along with violet shorts carried over from their second kit.<ref>{{Cite web |title=0-1: Premio al tesón del Pucela que jugó con camiseta y mediaas amarillas y pantalón violeta de la segunda equipación.{{!}} Real Valladolid C.F. |url=https://www.realvalladolid.es/noticias/0-1-premio-al-teson |access-date=2023-09-24 |website=Real Valladolid C.F. - Web Oficial |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Resumen y gol del Real Oviedo vs. Real Valladolid CF, jornada 7.{{!}} Diario As |url=https://as.com/futbol/videos/resumen-y-gol-del-real-oviedo-vs-real-valladolid-cf-jornada-7-de-laliga-hypermotion-v/ |access-date=2023-09-24 |website=Diario As - Web Oficial |date=24 September 2023 |language=es}}</ref>

